    "limitations": "Out-of-sample: each forecast uses only prices settled before its origin, and every model is refitted at every origin. Origins step by elapsed half-hours, so they shift by an hour of local time across a clock change. Intervals are model-based; WMAPE and sMAPE are fractions. A fold with a missing price in its window or targets is excluded, not imputed. Not a probability of a price spike or a trading signal. The seasonal naive's intervals are scored but not stored as series. The ensemble averages each interval bound (quantile averaging), which does not recalibrate coverage. Diebold-Mariano p-values test equal accuracy over these folds only; with about 56 errors per lead and heavy-tailed prices they are approximate, and testing several models and leads at once makes some small p-values likely by chance.",
